          %h2#section_Idea Idea
          %p
            Rough Paths are a way of defining
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stieltjes+integral"} Riemann-Stieltjes type integrals
            for paths with poor
            = succeed "-variation" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+equations"} differential equations
          %p
          %h2#section_Set-Up Set-Up
          %p We want to solve differential equations of the form:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi y
                    %mi t
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi y
                    %mn 0
                  %mo +
                  %msubsup
                    %mo ∫
                    %mn 0
                    %mi t
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi y
                    %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msub
                    %mi dX
                    %mi s
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  y_t=y_0+\int_0^t V(y_s)\otimes dX_s
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi V
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mo .
                  %mo .
                  %mo .
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi V
                    %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V=(V_1,...,V_d)
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi V
                    %mi i
                  %mo ∈
                  %msubsup
                    %mi C
                    %mi b
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi d
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_i\in C_b^\infty(\mathbb{R}^d,\mathbb{R}^d)
            smooth bounded vector fields and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                  %mi f
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo −
                      %mi var
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi sup
                    %mi 𝒫
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi t
                  %mo −
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi s
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi p
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi p
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\in C^p([0,T],\mathbb{R}^d)=\{f\colon \|f\|_{p-var}\colon = (\sup_{\mathcal{P}} |f_t-f_s|^p)^{1/p}\lt \infty\}
            is a signal with finite
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            variation.
          %p We want to solve this by a fixed point argument/Picard iteration. That means we must define:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mo ∫
                    %mn 0
                    %mi t
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msub
                    %mi dX
                    %mi s
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\int_0^t f(X_s)\otimes dX_s
          %p
            for smooth bounded
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
          %p
            The classical paper (
            %a{:href => "#Young36"}> Young 1936
            ) says, in short, that one can define this integral as a Riemann-Stieltjes integral iff
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p\lt 2
          %p
            A theorem by Bichdeller-Dellecherie says, in short, that one can define this
            %span.newWikiWord
              integral in Itô sense
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/It%C3%B4+integral"} ?
            if and only if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %span.newWikiWord
                semimartingale
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/semimartingale"} ?
          %p
          %h2#section_Main_Result Main Result
          %p
            Given a sequence of partitions,
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
